---
// Support page — the "Support URL" for the App Store and Google Play listings.
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title="SharedCue Support" description="Get help with SharedCue: guides, common questions, and how to contact us." />
		<style>
			main {
				width: 720px;
			}
			h1 {
				margin-bottom: 0.2em;
				font-size: 2.2em;
			}
			.lede {
				margin-top: 0;
				color: rgb(var(--gray));
			}
			h2 {
				margin: 1.6em 0 0.4em;
				font-size: 1.35em;
			}
			h3 {
				margin: 1.2em 0 0.2em;
				font-size: 1.05em;
			}
			.contact {
				padding: 1em 1.25em;
				border-radius: 12px;
				background: white;
				box-shadow: var(--box-shadow);
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>SharedCue Support</h1>
			<p class="lede">Help with setting up and using SharedCue.</p>

			<div class="contact">
				<strong>Contact us:</strong> <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a><br />
				Tell us the phone model you're using and what happened, and we'll get back to you.
			</div>

			<h2>Guides</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><a href="/blog/what-is-sharedcue/">What is SharedCue, and how can it help?</a></li>
				<li><a href="/blog/getting-started-with-sharedcue/">SharedCue features and how to use them</a></li>
				<li><a href="/blog/5-ways-to-use-sharedcue/">5 everyday ways to use SharedCue</a></li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Common questions</h2>

			<h3>How do I sign in?</h3>
			<p>
				Enter your mobile number and tap <strong>Send code</strong>, then type the 6-digit code from
				your messages and tap <strong>Verify</strong>. There's no password.
			</p>

			<h3>I invited someone, but they didn't get the invitation.</h3>
			<p>
				The other person needs to install SharedCue and sign up with that exact mobile number first,
				then you can send the invite again. On their phone, the invitation appears at the top of Home;
				if it isn't there yet, they can tap the refresh button at the top right.
			</p>

			<h3>Can I share my Personal group?</h3>
			<p>
				No. <strong>Personal</strong> is just for you. To share with someone, create a new group with
				<strong>+ Add Group</strong> and invite them to it.
			</p>

			<h3>Why can't I rename or delete a group?</h3>
			<p>
				Only the person who created a group can rename or delete it. Anyone in the group can add,
				edit and check off items, and rename or delete lists.
			</p>

			<h3>My reminders don't alert me.</h3>
			<p>
				Make sure notifications are allowed for SharedCue in your phone's Settings. The reminder time is
				saved either way.
			</p>

			<h3>Does SharedCue work offline?</h3>
			<p>
				Yes. Keep adding and checking off items; if you see <strong>Waiting</strong>, your changes will
				send when you're back online.
			</p>

			<h3>How do I change the app's language?</h3>
			<p>Tap your initial at the top right of Home to open <strong>Profile</strong>, then tap <strong>Language</strong>.</p>

			<h3>How do I delete my account?</h3>
			<p>See <a href="/delete-account/">Delete your SharedCue account</a>.</p>

			<h2>Privacy</h2>
			<p>Read our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
